{"format_version": 2, "segments": [{"kind": "text", "text": "εἰλίπους [ι^], ὁ, ἡ, πουν, τό , gen. ποδος· (εἴλω, πούς):— rolling in their gait, in"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hom.", "author_abbreviation": "Hom.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "(only in dat. and acc. pl.,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Il. 6.424", "author_abbreviation": "Il.", "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ","}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "9.466", "author_abbreviation": null, "tlg_author": "0012", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ") as epith. of oxen, which bring round their hind legs with a circling or rolling motion, cf."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Hp. Art. 8", "author_abbreviation": "Hp.", "tlg_author": "0627", "tlg_work": "010", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; εἰλίποδες, abs., for oxen or kine,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Theoc. 25.131", "author_abbreviation": "Theoc.", "tlg_author": "0005", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; also of women, having a rolling gait,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Eup. 161", "author_abbreviation": "Eup.", "tlg_author": "0461", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; also expld. sens. obsc.,"}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Anacr. 164", "author_abbreviation": "Anacr.", "tlg_author": "0237", "tlg_work": "001", "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", cf."}, {"kind": "citation", "text": "Paus.Gr. Fr. 154", "author_abbreviation": "Paus.Gr.", "tlg_author": null, "tlg_work": null, "dialects": []}, {"kind": "text", "text": "; cf. ἀνελλίπους."}]}